Subject: defer blocking-send wait setup

Only sets up the blocking-send wait state once the connection is actually known
to be full, instead of on every send. A receiver that has disconnected or closed
its channel cannot drain its queue, so building the timer and adaptive wait for
it is wasted work that delays a failure the caller could have had immediately.

Keeps the numbering of the Holoscan SDK series it comes from, but not all of it:
the SDK's 0003 and 0004 are deliberately absent, so this carries only the send
path and not the hunk that advanced the SDK's private package-variant marker,
which describes a package this is not. 0003 renames the built artifacts and
narrows the exported targets to support the SDK's vendored build; 0004 only
softens a message() in a top-level CMakeLists.txt these recipes never configure.
Neither is needed to build or use the callbacks, which is the whole reason this
series can sit on the ordinary iceoryx2 recipes.

Derived from Holoscan SDK 5.0.0,
public/cmake/deps/patches/iceoryx2/0003-defer-blocking-send-wait-setup.patch

Upstream-Status: Pending

